  "scope": "A disposable Kind cluster runs two Zot v2.1.23 registries with identical fixture accounts: a permissive baseline and a scoped policy. A running Kubernetes inference client receives only a case-owned read credential; a publisher can read/create in training/model; and a separate steward can read/create/update/delete there. The registry enforces authentication and repository/action decisions at OCI Distribution manifest and model blob endpoints. The Kubernetes service account labels/binds the inference workload only; it is not federated to Zot. This does not test OIDC/IAM federation, Harbor/MLflow/Hugging Face Hub, real model payloads, production TLS/secret management, human-role governance, or deployed registry operations.",
